Carafe bench: a graphics channel sends subchannel 4 to the copy engine without SET_OBJECT, as GM20B
does. The hardware maps subchannels to engines by a fixed rule and subchannel 4 of a graphics
channel is its copy engine; SET_OBJECT only checks the class. NVK relies on that: it binds 3D and
compute itself and sends every vkCmdCopy* (texture uploads, buffer copies) on subchannel 4 without
binding it, so Eden dropped all of them ("Method 0xc0 on subchannel 4 with no engine bound").
A SET_OBJECT from the guest, as NVN, deko3d and Mesa nvc0 send, still rebinds the subchannel.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

diff --git a/src/video_core/control/channel_state.cpp b/src/video_core/control/channel_state.cpp
index d07c7e2..b7f6e46 100644
